# The town's comings and goings. The format is described at the top of scripts/story.gd.
# Every line here is a draft for Alex.
#
# Gary from Willow Homes calls at the farm (main.gd _update_gary_visit fires "gary_visit"): the
# first time on her second day, while she's home between ten and four, to introduce himself and
# pitch the three plots on his books (data/economy.json "land"), all far out of her reach; then
# every two weeks (GARY_EVERY) with another pitch about trading up. Buying land isn't in yet.

== gary_intro
@trigger event gary_visit
@once
@fade out 0.6
@place nora 9.8 6.6 90
@place gary 11.6 4.8 270
@face gary nora
@face nora gary
@camera between gary nora 7 yaw 45
@fade in 0.8
> A car she hasn't heard before. Shoes far too clean for a farm track pick their way up to the gate.
Gary (happy): Morning! Don't get up. Well, you're up. Gary, Willow Homes. We met on your tour. You'll remember the hair.
Nora (wry): I remember the blazer.
Gary (wry): Everyone does. So. Birchfield. Charming. Rustic. "Character." That's estate-agent for draughty.
Gary (neutral): I'm not here to sell you anything. I'm here to show you what you'll want to buy. Three listings, exclusive to me.
Gary (happy): Eastfield Acres, the meadows east of town. Twenty flat acres of sweet grass. Room for a hundred sheep. Twelve and a half thousand.
Gary (warm): Greyspine Hollow, up in the foothills. A stone cottage, a spring, a view of the whole range. Twenty-one thousand.
Gary (happy): And Saltmeadow Point. The bluff above the beach, sea on three sides. Thirty-six thousand. The crown jewel.
? He waits, smiling, like a man who has never once been told no.
- I've got about forty coins and two sheep. -> broke | familiarity gary +2
- They sound lovely. Maybe one day. -> dream | familiarity gary +3; trust gary +1
@label broke
Gary (wry): Then you're my favourite kind of client: one with a long future. I'll keep them warm for you. Ish.
@goto bye
@label dream
Gary (warm): One day is my favourite day. It's when everyone buys.
@label bye
Gary (neutral): I'll swing by every couple of weeks. Keep the porch swept. Buyers judge porches.
@set gary_met
@walk gary 24 4.4 nowait
@wait 1.6
@home gary off
@toast Gary's land listings are on his menu at Willow Homes.
@camera player

== gary_pitch
@trigger event gary_visit
@requires gary_met
@fade out 0.6
@place nora 9.8 6.6 90
@place gary 11.6 4.8 270
@face gary nora
@face nora gary
@camera between gary nora 7 yaw 45
@fade in 0.8
Gary (happy): Me again! Don't look so thrilled. I was passing. I'm never passing. I came specially.
@if hearts gary >= 2 -> friendly
Gary (wry): Still the starter farm, I see. Cozy. Small. Nobody's judging. I'm judging a little.
@goto pitch
@label friendly
Gary (warm): Place is looking good, actually. Don't tell anyone I said that. It ruins my whole approach.
@label pitch
Gary (neutral): Eastfield Acres is still on my books. Greyspine Hollow and Saltmeadow Point too. Nobody in this town can afford them. Except, one day, you.
Gary (happy): Think about it. Trading up. Room to grow. A gate with your name on it.
Nora (wry): I'll think about it.
Gary (wry): That's what they all say, right before they do it.
@walk gary 24 4.4 nowait
@wait 1.6
@home gary off
@camera player
